y":"Buy the Screenshot Evidence Check skill file (SKILL.md)","description":"Reads a description of how a web page was captured or measured - a headless browser capture with a window size, a tall screenshot, a document width reading, a local Lighthouse run, a PageSpeed Insights run, an automation session that has been open for hours, a command-line download size on Windows - and says what that evidence proves, what it cannot prove and the one measurement that would decide, answered as JSON with a verdict. Knows the ways the capture itself produces the symptom - headless windows under about 500 pixels that lay out wider and crop the picture, no touch emulation behind a window-size flag, blank images in very tall captures, scroll-reveal sections caught before they appear, a width reading that stays clean while a container clips, scores that move with machine load, a long automation session that stops running page scripts, a download size of zero at a successful status. Use when an agent or a person is about to report that a page is broken or fixed from a screenshot, a score or a command-line reading. One-time purchase of the SKILL.md file: you pay once, keep it forever, and re-download it and get new versions free with the token from the 200 answer.","tags":["payment"],"security":[],"parameters":[{"name":"x402Version","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Force the older protocol version. Only for clients that speak x402 v1.","schema":{"type":"integer","enum":[1,2],"default":2}}],"x-payment-info":{"protocols":[{"x402":{}}],"price":{"mode":"fixed","currency":"USD","amount":"0.03"},"network":"base","asset":"USDC","payTo":"0x8e37022edcf0f21cf3c9f93fee9d4d32519f36f4"},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Payment settled. JSON with file.content (the SKILL.md text), sha256, receipt and redownload.token (shown once)."},"402":{"description":"Payment required. The requirements travel in the PAYMENT-REQUIRED header (base64 JSON, x402 v2) and in the body. Nothing is charged by a 402. Also returned when the till is closed (selling: false): then do not sign."},"404":{"description":"skill_not_found: no such skill, or it is not sold as a file."},"409":{"description":"payment_in_progress: the same payment is being processed. Retry the identical header; nothing was charged twice. already_paid: this authorization was already settled - do NOT sign a new one. A replayed header returns the file only within 60 s of purchase and only when signed by the paying wallet; otherwise the reply carries the receipt, not the file. Use the redownload token from your first response."},"429":{"description":"rate_limited: wait retry_after_seconds. The per-wallet limit counts only fresh authorizations whose signature recovers to that wallet; a header carrying your address with someone else's signature, or a replay of an already-settled authorization, does not count against you. reason lane_hourly_ceiling: our own hourly ceiling on fresh attempts toward the payment facilitator (per signature lane, not per wallet) is reached; the reply carries lane and Retry-After, the number of seconds until the top of the next UTC hour. Nothing was charged and the nonce is not spent - resend the identical header after that, re-sign only if it has expired."},"500":{"description":"Branch on `error` and `retryable`. file_missing / file_corrupt (retryable: true): the payment is recorded; resend the identical payment header later and you get the file without a second charge. payment_accepted_not_delivered (retryable: false): do NOT sign a new authorization; quote the nonce from the body, we reconcile by hand."},"503":{"description":"not_selling, facilitator_unavailable or temporarily_unavailable: nothing was settled; retry later."}}}},"/v1/skills/chain-evidence-check/file":{"get":{"operationId":"buy_chain_evidence_check","summary":"Buy the Chain Evidence Check skill file (SKILL.md)","description":"Judges whether an on-chain observation really proves a claim about a payment, a wallet or an RPC endpoint on an EVM chain, and answers as JSON with a binary verdict, the reason and the one check that would decide. Knows the readings that answer for the wrong thing - a null transaction receipt seconds after settlement, a block explorer that indexes a minute late and a balance view that lags its own transfer list, a public RPC endpoint that refuses receipts with an error or with an HTML page behind status 200, a reader that returns zero when the call failed, a chain of endpoints that says ok when two of three are dead, a transfer of the right amount that matches three open orders, a payment header copied from public calldata - and the readings that do prove it. Use when an agent says paid, settled, not found, reverted, empty, missing funds or endpoint dead from chain data and you need to know whether its evidence supports that. One-time purchase of the SKILL.md file: you pay once, keep it forever, and re-download it and get new versions free with the token from the 200 answer.","tags":["payment"],"security":[],"parameters":[{"name":"x402Version","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Force the older protocol version. Only for clients that speak x402 v1.","schema":{"type":"integer","enum":[1,2],"default":2}}],"x-payment-info":{"protocols":[{"x402":{}}],"price":{"mode":"fixed","currency":"USD","amount":"0.05"},"network":"base","asset":"USDC","payTo":"0x8e37022edcf0f21cf3c9f93fee9d4d32519f36f4"},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Payment settled. JSON with file.content (the SKILL.md text), sha256, receipt and redownload.token (shown once)."},"402":{"description":"Payment required. The requirements travel in the PAYMENT-REQUIRED header (base64 JSON, x402 v2) and in the body. Nothing is charged by a 402. Also returned when the till is closed (selling: false): then do not sign."},"404":{"description":"skill_not_found: no such skill, or it is not sold as a file."},"409":{"description":"payment_in_progress: the same payment is being processed. Retry the identical header; nothing was charged twice. already_paid: this authorization was already settled - do NOT sign a new one. A replayed header returns the file only within 60 s of purchase and only when signed by the paying wallet; otherwise the reply carries the receipt, not the file. Use the redownload token from your first response."},"429":{"description":"rate_limited: wait retry_after_seconds. The per-wallet limit counts only fresh authorizations whose signature recovers to that wallet; a header carrying your address with someone else's signature, or a replay of an already-settled authorization, does not count against you. reason lane_hourly_ceiling: our own hourly ceiling on fresh attempts toward the payment facilitator (per signature lane, not per wallet) is reached; the reply carries lane and Retry-After, the number of seconds until the top of the next UTC hour. Nothing was charged and the nonce is not spent - resend the identical header after that, re-sign only if it has expired."},"500":{"description":"Branch on `error` and `retryable`. file_missing / file_corrupt (retryable: true): the payment is recorded; resend the identical payment header later and you get the file without a second charge. payment_accepted_not_delivered (retryable: false): do NOT sign a new authorization; quote the nonce from the body, we reconcile by hand."},"503":{"description":"not_selling, facilitator_unavailable or temporarily_unavailable: nothing was settled; retry later."}}}},"/v1/skills/yaml-repair/file":{"get":{"operationId":"buy_yaml_repair","summary":"Buy the YAML Repair: Fix Broken YAML, Keep Every Value skill file (SKILL.md)","description":"Repairs broken YAML and Markdown front matter so a program can parse it, without changing any value's text or type, and answers with the YAML only, no code fence. Fixes tabs used as indentation, indentation that fits no parent, a missing closing quote or bracket, values that need quotes (a colon inside, a leading star or at sign), and output cut off in the middle, where the cut value is kept as cut and never completed. Yes, no, on, off and NO stay strings, 1,250 stays a string, 1.10 and 01234 stay as written. Duplicate keys, input that is not YAML, and input with two readings get a fixed one-line answer instead of a guess. Use when a tool, an API or another model returned YAML or front matter that does not parse, or when asked to fix, clean up or close invalid or truncated YAML. One-time purchase of the SKILL.md file: you pay once, keep it forever, and re-download it and get new versions free with the token from the 200 answer.","tags":["payment"],"security":[],"parameters":[{"name":"x402Version","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Force the older protocol version. Only for clients that speak x402 v1.","schema":{"type":"integer","enum":[1,2],"default":2}}],"x-payment-info":{"protocols":[{"x402":{}}],"price":{"mode":"fixed","currency":"USD","amount":"0.05"},"network":"base","asset":"USDC","payTo":"0x8e37022edcf0f21cf3c9f93fee9d4d32519f36f4"},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Payment settled. JSON with file.content (the SKILL.md text), sha256, receipt and redownload.token (shown once)."},"402":{"description":"Payment required. The requirements travel in the PAYMENT-REQUIRED header (base64 JSON, x402 v2) and in the body. Nothing is charged by a 402. Also returned when the till is closed (selling: false): then do not sign."},"404":{"description":"skill_not_found: no such skill, or it is not sold as a file."},"409":{"description":"payment_in_progress: the same payment is being processed. Retry the identical header; nothing was charged twice. already_paid: this authorization was already settled - do NOT sign a new one. A replayed header returns the file only within 60 s of purchase and only when signed by the paying wallet; otherwise the reply carries the receipt, not the file. Use the redownload token from your first response."},"429":{"description":"rate_limited: wait retry_after_seconds. The per-wallet limit counts only fresh authorizations whose signature recovers to that wallet; a header carrying your address with someone else's signature, or a replay of an already-settled authorization, does not count against you. reason lane_hourly_ceiling: our own hourly ceiling on fresh attempts toward the payment facilitator (per signature lane, not per wallet) is reached; the reply carries lane and Retry-After, the number of seconds until the top of the next UTC hour. Nothing was charged and the nonce is not spent - resend the identical header after that, re-sign only if it has expired."},"500":{"description":"Branch on `error` and `retryable`. file_missing / file_corrupt (retryable: true): the payment is recorded; resend the identical payment header later and you get the file without a second charge. payment_accepted_not_delivered (retryable: false): do NOT sign a new authorization; quote the nonce from the body, we reconcile by hand."},"503":{"description":"not_selling, facilitator_unavailable or temporarily_unavailable: nothing was settled; retry later."}}}},"/v1/skills/env-file-repair/file":{"get":{"operationId":"buy_env_file_repair","summary":"Buy the Env File Repair: Fix .env and INI Syntax, Keep Values skill file (SKILL.md)","description":"Repairs a broken .env file or INI file so the program that loads it reads every variable with the value its author meant, and answers with the file only, no code fence. Quotes a value that holds a hash sign or must keep its leading or trailing spaces, closes a quote that was left open, joins a key pasted over several lines, picks the quote style that keeps backslashes and mixed quotes intact, and leaves numbers such as 007 and 1.10, empty values and placeholders exactly as written. A key set twice to different values, a bare line that may be a lost key, a quote with two ways to close, and input that is JSON or another format get a one-line CANNOT REPAIR answer instead of a guess. Use when a config pasted from chat or mod