pt it. Only the msgstr values change. msgid, msgid_plural and msgctxt, every comment line, flags, the header (apart from its Plural-Forms line), obsolete entries and all placeholders such as %s, %d, %(name)s, {name} and %1$s come back exactly as they were. Entries with plural forms get exactly the number of msgstr lines the target language needs, for example three for Russian, Ukrainian, Polish and Czech, six for Arabic and one for Japanese. Use to translate or localize a .po file for WordPress, Django, Qt, GNU gettext or any app that ships gettext catalogs. One-time purchase of the SKILL.md file: you pay once, keep it forever, and re-download it and get new versions free with the token from the 200 answer.","tags":["payment"],"security":[],"parameters":[{"name":"x402Version","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Force the older protocol version. Only for clients that speak x402 v1.","schema":{"type":"integer","enum":[1,2],"default":2}}],"x-payment-info":{"protocols":[{"x402":{}}],"price":{"mode":"fixed","currency":"USD","amount":"0.02"},"network":"base","asset":"USDC","payTo":"0x8e37022edcf0f21cf3c9f93fee9d4d32519f36f4"},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Payment settled. JSON with file.content (the SKILL.md text), sha256, receipt and redownload.token (shown once)."},"402":{"description":"Payment required. The requirements travel in the PAYMENT-REQUIRED header (base64 JSON, x402 v2) and in the body. Nothing is charged by a 402. Also returned when the till is closed (selling: false): then do not sign."},"404":{"description":"skill_not_found: no such skill, or it is not sold as a file."},"409":{"description":"payment_in_progress: the same payment is being processed. Retry the identical header; nothing was charged twice. already_paid: this authorization was already settled - do NOT sign a new one. A replayed header returns the file only within 60 s of purchase and only when signed by the paying wallet; otherwise the reply carries the receipt, not the file. Use 